  "id": "cingulum-bundle",
  "term": "cingulum bundle",
  "definition": "The cingulum bundle is a major white matter pathway that runs from the front to the back of the brain and links frontal, parietal, and temporal regions. Because of its central position in brain networks, it is considered important for cognitive functioning, and age-related changes in this tract have been associated with problems in memory and executive function.",
